    "type": "text",
    "text": "Here's a compact bash version: `pg_dump` in custom format (already compressed), date-based rotation, logging to syslog.\n\n```bash\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nDB=\"shop\"\nDIR=\"/var/backups/postgres\"\nKEEP_DAYS=14\nFILE=\"$DIR/$DB-$(date +%F_%H%M).dump\"\n\nmkdir -p \"$DIR\"\npg_dump -Fc -Z 6 \"$DB\" -f \"$FILE\"\nfind \"$DIR\" -name \"$DB-*.dump\" -mtime +$KEEP_DAYS -delete\nlogger -t pg-backup \"ok: $FILE ($(du -h \"$FILE\" | cut -f1))\"\n```\n\nRun it daily at 03:30:\n\n```cron\n30 3 * * * postgres /usr/local/bin/pg-backup.sh\n```\n\nTo check that a dump is restorable: `pg_restore --list \"$FILE\" | head`.",
